@crew abara-rosa
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hi. Abara, Survey. The comics in the common room? Some of those are mine.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. You might be in the next one. Drawn kindly. Mostly.   #funny
- Hi, {me}. Scanner's free if you need it. I'm just labelling.
? tier>=friend
- Hey, {me}. I drew you. Holding a spanner. Looking heroic. Don't make it weird.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. New comic up. Three people laughed in front of it.
? mood:low
- Couldn't draw today. That's how I know it's a bad day.
== near
? habit:common-room
- The comics wall. Mine's the one with the lift that sulks.   #funny
? act:meal
- Our family stall on Valo did soup like this. Not as good. Don't tell Brennan.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I ran a market stall on Valo. All day, shouting prices. Now I whisper.   #funny
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- My comics. Little squares of life aboard. People find themselves in them, and smile.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 3: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, bye, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about, life)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}. I'm sketching the breakfast queue. You're in it. Small, at the back.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh. Hi, {me}. It's been a while. The comics wall's been short of good material.   #funny

== bye
- Bye. Mind how you go. If you trip, I might draw it.   #funny

== near
? habit:common-room
- The comics wall. Hart's got a new one up. Teague's sulking. Good week.   #funny
? habit:lingers-at-meals
- I stay after meals. People are funnier when they're full.

== invite
- Swap table tonight? I'm swapping comics for pencils. Bring something small.

== accept
- Yes. Okay. I'll bring my sketchbook.
- Yes. I'll come. I won't draw you. Probably.   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. I've a comic to finish. Another time?
? weekday:thu|fri
- Rest day. Pencils, common room, quiet. Saturday?

== missed
- You didn't come. That's fine. I drew the empty chair. It's very moving.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. There's a little comic on the wall. Third row. It's about you.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Teague and Hart drew me a comic. Two styles. One very confused me.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's in. I'll draw it after. Everyone holding on to their mugs.

== hint
- {me}. Have you a minute later? I've something to say. Out loud, not drawn.

== about
? aff:teague-theo:friend
- Teague and I share the comics wall. He's louder. I'm neater. It works.   #funny

== life
? tier>=friend
- On Valo I shouted prices all day. Drawing's quieter. I say more with it.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- That's a comic. Sketching.
- People are funnier after meals.
- Comics for pencils. A fair swap.
- Don't explain the comic.   #funny
? act:off
- Common room. Pencils. Quiet.
?

== rumour
- Out loud, not drawn: news.
- It'll be a comic. You hear it first.
